From: Jared Wyles <jared.wyles@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:12:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 21/32] skippy: trace K/V row-list runs

Each ubatch that fills row lists reports a llama.kv_rows span: the most
contiguous cell runs one list holds, with cells:runs per slice in its
detail, so a trace shows how fragmented the unified pool is for each query
slice. skippy_trace::active() lets that work run only while a span callback
is installed.

The row-list path is measured against ordinary attention over the unified
pool with llama.cpp's own LLAMA_KV_ROWS_DISABLE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QA3dWey3RBtBgDz1Tery9Y
